---
source: crates/rupu-agentiflow/tests/it/flow_toolset_parity.rs
expression: "unit_toolset(\"\").await"
---
- description: "Search the workspace by code STRUCTURE (syntax tree), not text, using ast-grep. Provide a `pattern` in ast-grep syntax and a `lang` (rust, python, typescript, go, …). Metavariables: `$VAR` matches one named node, `$$$` matches zero or more nodes. Example: pattern `impl $T for $S` with lang `rust` finds trait impls; pattern `async fn $NAME($$$) -> Result<$$$>` finds async fns returning Result. Output is `path:line:col: match` lines (1-based, workspace-relative). Prefer this over `grep` when you want syntactic matches (call sites, impls, signatures) instead of regex over raw text. `path` is relative to the workspace; an absolute `path` is allowed only inside a skill's base directory (`skills.load` returns it). Returns empty stdout (not an error) when there are no matches."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      lang:
        description: "Language grammar to parse with, e.g. `rust`, `python`, `typescript`, `go`, `javascript`, `java`, `c`, `cpp`. Required."
        type: string
      path:
        description: Optional sub-path within the workspace to restrict the search. Defaults to the whole workspace.
        type: string
      pattern:
        description: "Structural pattern in ast-grep syntax. Metavariables: `$VAR` = one node, `$$$` = zero-or-more nodes. Example: `impl $T for $S`."
        type: string
    required:
      - pattern
      - lang
    type: object
  name: ast_grep
- description: "Execute a shell command with `/bin/sh -c`, starting in the workspace directory. The command runs with a controlled environment (PATH, HOME, USER, TERM, LANG plus a per-workspace allowlist). A command that runs past the run's timeout (120 seconds unless configured) is killed and returns an error. Use this for compilation, tests, git operations, and anything else that needs a shell."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      command:
        description: "The shell command to execute, e.g. `cargo test`, `git diff HEAD`, `ls -la src/`."
        type: string
    required:
      - command
    type: object
  name: bash
- description: "Atomically claim a work unit so no other participant duplicates it. Returns granted, or the current holder when it is already claimed."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      work_unit:
        description: "Identifier of the unit of work to claim, e.g. host:1.1.2.2"
        type: string
    required:
      - work_unit
    type: object
  name: board.claim
- description: "Post to the shared board every participant can read: an observation, a question, an answer, a vote, or a note. Optionally address it to a participant (lynx#1), role:<agent>, step:<id>, parent or lead: an addressed post also lands in each addressee's inbox, so they see it on their next turn. Returns the post's `id` and who it was delivered to."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      addressed_to:
        description: "Who this post is for: a participant (lynx#1), role:<agent>, step:<id>, parent or lead; omit for everyone"
        type: string
      body:
        type: string
      kind:
        enum:
          - observation
          - question
          - answer
          - vote
          - note
        type: string
    required:
      - kind
      - body
    type: object
  name: board.post
- description: "Read the shared board's posts, oldest first, newest last. Returns the most recent posts (default 50); filter to those addressed to a participant id or role with addressed_to."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      addressed_to:
        description: Only posts addressed to this participant id or role
        type: string
      limit:
        description: Maximum posts to return (the most recent ones); default 50
        maximum: 500
        minimum: 1
        type: integer
    type: object
  name: board.read
- description: "Release a work unit you previously claimed with board.claim, so another participant can take it."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      work_unit:
        description: Identifier of the claimed unit of work to release
        type: string
    required:
      - work_unit
    type: object
  name: board.release
- description: "Start a child run and get a handle back at once; the child works on its own. `kind` picks how it runs: `subagent` (the default: in this process, for a quick delegation such as reviewing a file), `agent` (its own `rupu run` process, for long or heavy work), or `workflow` (its own `rupu workflow run`). Name an agent from your dispatchable agents, a workflow from your dispatchable workflows, or pass a `file` that `workflows.generate` returned. Call `join` with the handle to collect the result, or pass `wait: true` to start the child and wait for it in one call. Children you never join are stopped when you finish."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      file:
        description: "Kind `workflow` only: a workflow file `workflows.generate` returned, instead of `name`"
        type: string
      inputs:
        additionalProperties: true
        description: "A workflow's declared inputs as name: value pairs; for an agent, structured inputs added to its prompt"
        type: object
      kind:
        description: "How the child runs; default `subagent`"
        enum:
          - subagent
          - agent
          - workflow
        type: string
      name:
        description: "The agent (or, for kind `workflow`, the workflow) to run"
        type: string
      prompt:
        description: "An agent child's task: what to do and what to report back"
        type: string
      timeout_secs:
        description: "With `wait`: how long to wait, in seconds; default 300"
        maximum: 3600
        minimum: 0
        type: integer
      wait:
        description: Wait for the child to finish and return its result too; default false
        type: boolean
    type: object
  name: dispatch
- description: "Replace an exact string in a file. The `old_string` must match exactly once in the file; if it matches zero times or more than once, the edit fails. Pass enough surrounding context (a few lines before/after) to make `old_string` uniquely identifying. The file must already exist; for new files use `write_file`."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      new_string:
        description: Replacement substring.
        type: string
      old_string:
        description: Exact substring to replace. Must match exactly once.
        type: string
      path:
        description: Path relative to the workspace root.
        type: string
    required:
      - path
      - old_string
      - new_string
    type: object
  name: edit_file
- description: "List files in the workspace matching a glob pattern. Output is one path per line, sorted, relative to the workspace root. Supports `**` for recursive descent. Patterns are relative to the workspace; an absolute pattern is allowed only inside a skill's base directory (`skills.load` returns it), and its matches are absolute. Returns empty stdout when nothing matches."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      pattern:
        description: "Glob pattern, e.g. `src/**/*.rs` or `*.toml`."
        type: string
    required:
      - pattern
    type: object
  name: glob
- description: "Search the workspace for a pattern using ripgrep. Output is `path:line:match` lines, gitignore-aware. Use this to locate symbols, callers, or any text across the workspace. `path` is relative to the workspace; an absolute `path` is allowed only inside a skill's base directory (`skills.load` returns it). Returns empty stdout (not an error) when there are no matches."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      path:
        description: Optional sub-path within the workspace to restrict the search. Defaults to the whole workspace.
        type: string
      pattern:
        description: "Regex pattern to search for. Ripgrep's default regex syntax (similar to PCRE)."
        type: string
    required:
      - pattern
    type: object
  name: grep
- description: "Wait for children you started with `dispatch` and collect their results. Name `handles` (omit them for every child you have not collected yet). Returns each child's status: `done` (with its output and whether it succeeded), `failed`, `abandoned`, or `running` / `pending` if it has not finished within the timeout (join again to keep waiting). `until: any` returns as soon as one of them finishes."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      handles:
        description: "Handles `dispatch` returned; omit for every child of this run not yet joined"
        items:
          type: string
        type: array
      timeout_secs:
        description: "How long to wait, in seconds (0 = just look); default 300"
        maximum: 3600
        minimum: 0
        type: integer
      until:
        description: "Return when all of them have finished (default), or any one"
        enum:
          - all
          - any
        type: string
    type: object
  name: join
- description: "Send a message. `to` is a participant (lynx#1) or its full codename, role:<agent> or step:<id> (every live participant running it), \"parent\", \"lead\", \"operator\", or \"broadcast\" (every participant sees it once, from the moment it started listening; the broadcast log is capped, so don't spam it). Recipients see it before their next model call. Returns the message's `id` and who it reached; `undelivered` says who it didn't, and why."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      body:
        type: string
      to:
        description: "Recipient: a participant, role:<agent>, step:<id>, parent, lead, operator or broadcast"
        type: string
    required:
      - to
      - body
    type: object
  name: msg.send
- description: "Read a file from the workspace and return its contents prefixed by 1-based line numbers separated by tabs. Always use this before editing a file so you have current line numbers. Paths are relative to the workspace root and may not leave the workspace, except into a skill's base directory (`skills.load` returns it), which may be given as an absolute path."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      path:
        description: "Path relative to the workspace root, e.g. `src/lib.rs` or `tests/foo.rs`."
        type: string
    required:
      - path
    type: object
  name: read_file
- description: "Create a file or overwrite an existing one in the workspace. Use this for new files; for edits to existing files prefer `edit_file` to preserve unrelated content. Intermediate directories are created as needed. Paths must be inside the workspace root."
  input_schema:
    properties:
      content:
        description: Full content of the file. Existing content is replaced.
        type: string
      path:
        description: Path relative to the workspace root.
        type: string
    required:
      - path
      - content
    type: object
  name: write_file
